-- title:
--   One Le Ld Pasting Nu Of Large Zeta
-- statement:
--   **A large family consistency error makes the pasting scale at least one.** Let `strategy` be a symmetric strategy at the successor parameters, assume it is good for $\varepsilon,\delta,\gamma$, and let $1\le k$. Write $N$ for the section-local pasting parameter. If
--
--   $$
--   1<\zeta,
--   $$
--
--   then
--
--   $$
--   1\le N.
--   $$
--
--   Goodness supplies nonnegativity of the three strategy test errors, while the $1/32$-power contribution from $\zeta$ is at least one. The remaining degree-ratio term is nonnegative, so the five-term lower-bound result yields the conclusion. This is the large-consistency-error branch used by `ldPasting`.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.one_le_ldPastingNu_of_large_zeta`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
